    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A loop ABCDA , carrying current $\\mathrm{I}=12 \\mathrm{~A}$, is placed in a plane, consists of two semi-circular segments of radius $R_1=6 \\pi \\mathrm{~m}$ and $\\mathrm{R}_2=4 \\pi \\mathrm{~m}$. The magnitude of the resultant magnetic field at center O is $\\mathrm{k} \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~T}$. The value of k is ______ (Given $\\mu_0=4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{Tm} \\mathrm{A}^{-1}$)<br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0014_79c67ebc3461.png\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Magnetic field due to $\\mathrm{AB} \\& \\mathrm{CD}=0$<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{B}_0=\\left|\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\mathrm{B}_{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right| \\\\\n& =\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{I}}{4 \\mathrm{R}_2}-\\frac{\\mu_0 \\mathrm{I}}{4 \\mathrm{R}_1} \\\\\n& =\\frac{4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\times 12}{4}\\left(\\frac{1}{4 \\pi}-\\frac{1}{6 \\pi}\\right) \\\\\n& =12 \\pi \\times 10^{-7}\\left(\\frac{1}{12 \\pi}\\right) \\\\\n& =1 \\times 10^{-7}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>$K=1$"
  }
}